      "content": "It sounds like you may be experiencing symptoms of hyperglycemia. Before taking sugar-lowering medication, check your blood sugar again with a glucose meter. Hyperglycemia can potentially cause symptoms like shakiness, sweating, and dizziness, but your response may vary. Consult with a healthcare provider for personalized advice. In the meantime, stay safe and monitor your blood glucose closely.",
